//
// A HOLE IN A TOKEN MATCH NAMES THE MISSING VARIANTS (`@FR-M-Exhaust`).  M-Exhaust: a match on
// an enum covers every variant or carries a `_`; a match missing one is a STATIC ERROR naming
// what is missing.  The compiler's own use: adding a token kind must break every match that
// forgot it, and the message must say which — here two of six are missing, both named, in
// declaration order.  The OCaml bar's C6 family (loft-lang/plans#202, probe `c9`).
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: match on Tok is not exhaustive — missing: Minus, RParen
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 9121f1b50, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names both missing variants.
// HOLDS: `M-Total/unit-arms-cover-an-enum-without-a-wildcard`, the covered half.

enum Tok { Ident { s: text }, Num { v: integer }, Plus, Minus, LParen, RParen }

fn show(t: Tok) -> text {
  match t {
    Ident { s } => s,
    Num { v } => "{v}",
    Plus => "+",
    LParen => "(",
  }
}

fn main() {
  assert(show(Plus) == "+", "unreachable");
}
